@startuml
title Sequence Diagram - UC-10 - Configure Timer Profiles

autonumber
actor Learner
participant "Desktop UI" as UI
participant "SettingsController" as Controller
participant "ManageTimerProfilesUseCase" as UseCase
participant "AppSettingsRepository" as Repo
participant "AppSettings" as Settings
participant "TimerProfile" as Profile
participant "SettingsMapper" as Mapper

Learner -> UI : create, edit, delete profile or select default
alt Create, edit or delete a profile
  UI -> Controller : POST /api/v1/settings/profiles or PUT/DELETE /api/v1/settings/profiles/{profileId}
  Controller -> UseCase : manageProfile(command)
else Select default profile
  UI -> Controller : PUT /api/v1/settings/profiles/default\n{profileId}
  Controller -> UseCase : selectDefault(profileId)
end
UseCase -> Repo : load()
Repo --> UseCase : AppSettings
UseCase -> Profile : create copy / validate preferences
Profile --> UseCase : validated profile
UseCase -> Settings : add, update, select or remove profile
Settings --> UseCase : updated
UseCase -> Repo : save(settings)
Repo --> UseCase : saved
UseCase -> Mapper : toDto(settings)
Mapper --> UseCase : SettingsDto
UseCase --> Controller : SettingsDto
Controller --> UI : 200 OK\n{...}

note over Profile
  Validation rules:
  - work: 1..180 minutes
  - short break: 1..60 minutes
  - long break: 1..120 minutes
  - intervalsBeforeLongBreak: 1..12
  - long break >= short break
  - profile name is trimmed, non-empty and case-insensitively unique
  - at least one profile remains; select a new default before deleting
    the current default
  - new profiles copy the current default profile
end note

note over Settings
  Timer profiles include independent work and break auto-start flags.
  Settings changes apply to new sessions; active sessions keep their
  snapshotted settings.
end note

@enduml
